note('Author page 17; archive 35. Derives (60) by inverting the alpha/tilde-alpha identity, giving (61), then substituting the inverse of (55) and setting zeta prime = eta zeta. The written reference is (75bis), although (25bis) appears intended; it is not silently corrected. The two rho exponents in (60) are overwritten and are represented as uncertain cancelled minus-ones. Local algebra confirms the live rho: from tilde alpha prime = rho^{-1}(zeta) zeta^{-1}, (61) gives alpha prime = eta zeta rho(zeta^{-1}eta^{-1}) = zeta prime rho(zeta prime)^{-1}, assuming the stated automorphism action. This check supports, but does not replace, the observed cancellation. The summary introduces triples (62) and ends with the author’s question mark after “relation des lacets”. The interleaved cancelled and inserted wording before the alpha-prime display remains uncertain in its small formula number.')
